    {
      "text": "###Data Representation in DataFrames and Datasets\nDataFrames are more than RDDs of Row objects; DataFrames and Datasets have a specialized\nrepresentation and columnar cache format. The specialized representation is not only more space\nefficient, but also can be much faster to encode than even Kryo serialization. To be clear, like RDDs,\nDataFrames and Datasets are generally lazily evaluated and build up a lineage of their\ndependencies (except in DataFrames this is called a logical plan and contains more information)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "820dc4dbc57d4f6fa3b2e"
    },
