      },
      "id": "9a332ac17d35419395e74"
    },
    {
      "text": "###DataFrames, Datasets, and Spark SQL\n\n\n- Like RDDs, DataFrames and Datasets represent distributed collections, with additional schema\ninformation not found in RDDs. This additional schema information  is used to provide a more\n\n- efficient storage layer (Tungsten), and in the optimizer (Catalyst) to perform additional optimizations.\nBeyond schema information, the operations performed on Datasets and DataFrames are such that\nthe optimizer can inspect the logical meaning rather than arbitrary functions. DataFrames are\nDatasets of a special Row object, which doesn’t provide any compile-time type checking",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "7b45b08047fe47b685bbe"
    },
